Host-side test harness for the iPod nano 3G FTL (ftl-nano3g.c).

sim_nand.c implements the nand-target.h API on an in-memory two-die NAND
that flags double programming and bad-block access; harness.c formats a
simulated flash with the FTL's own context writers, then runs write, sync,
wear-swap, unclean-remount (restore) and fault-injection scenarios against
a reference model and checks the pool invariants after each step.

Run: ./build.sh        (add -v for the FTL's DEBUGF output)
